    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Two new compounds could reveal hidden drivers of Alzheimer’s disease",
      "url": "https://sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/08/260802223437.htm",
      "summary": "Vanderbilt researchers created the first selective compound designed to inhibit TAOK-1, a poorly understood protein connected to Alzheimer’s disease. They also discovered a second compound that activates the entire TAOK protein family, offering scientists an unexpected new research tool. Together, the compounds could reveal hidden disease mechanisms and point toward new treatment strategies.",
